{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "KJV1769",
  "book_code": "LUK",
  "chapter": 24,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now upon the first ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the week, very early in the morning, they came unto the sepulchre, bringing the spices which they had prepared, and certain ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "others",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they found the stone rolled away from the sepulchre.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they entered in, and found not the body of the Lord Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, as they were much perplexed thereabout, behold, two men stood by them in shining garments:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as they were afraid, and bowed down ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " faces to the earth, they said unto them, Why seek ye the living among the dead?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He is not here, but is risen: remember how he spake unto you when he was yet in Galilee,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Saying, The Son of man must be delivered into the hands of sinful men, and be crucified, and the third day rise again.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they remembered his words,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And returned from the sepulchre, and told all these things unto the eleven, and to all the rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It was Mary Magdalene, and Joanna, and Mary ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the mother",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of James, and other ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "women that were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with them, which told these things unto the apostles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And their words seemed to them as idle tales, and they believed them not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then arose Peter, and ran unto the sepulchre; and stooping down, he beheld the linen clothes laid by themselves, and departed, wondering in himself at that which was come to pass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "¶ And, behold, two of them went that same day to a village called Emmaus, which was from Jerusalem ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "about",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " threescore furlongs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they talked together of all these things which had happened.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, that, while they communed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "together",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " and reasoned, Jesus himself drew near, and went with them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But their eyes were holden that they should not know him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, What manner of communications ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " these that ye have one to another, as ye walk, and are sad?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the one of them, whose name was Cleopas, answering said unto him, Art thou only a stranger in Jerusalem, and hast not known the things which are come to pass there in these days?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, What things? And they said unto him, Concerning Jesus of Nazareth, which was a prophet mighty in deed and word before God and all the people:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And how the chief priests and our rulers delivered him to be condemned to death, and have crucified him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But we trusted that it had been he which should have redeemed Israel: and beside all this, to day is the third day since these things were done.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yea, and certain women also of our company made us astonished, which were early at the sepulchre;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they found not his body, they came, saying, that they had also seen a vision of angels, which said that he was alive.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And certain of them which were with us went to the sepulchre, and found ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " even so as the women had said: but him they saw not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he said unto them, O fools, and slow of heart to believe all that the prophets have spoken:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ought not Christ to have suffered these things, and to enter into his glory?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And beginning at Moses and all the prophets, he expounded unto them in all the scriptures the things concerning himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they drew nigh unto the village, whither they went: and he made as though he would have gone further.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But they constrained him, saying, Abide with us: for it is toward evening, and the day is far spent. And he went in to tarry with them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, as he sat at meat with them, he took bread, and blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and brake, and gave to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And their eyes were opened, and they knew him; and he vanished out of their sight.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they said one to another, Did not our heart burn within us, while he talked with us by the way, and while he opened to us the scriptures?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they rose up the same hour, and returned to Jerusalem, and found the eleven gathered together, and them that were with them,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Saying, The Lord is risen indeed, and hath appeared to Simon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they told what things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were done",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the way, and how he was known of them in breaking of bread.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "¶ And as they thus spake, Jesus himself stood in the midst of them, and saith unto them, Peace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " unto you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But they were terrified and affrighted, and supposed that they had seen a spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, Why are ye troubled? and why do thoughts arise in your hearts?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold my hands and my feet, that it is I myself: handle me, and see; for a spirit hath not flesh and bones, as ye see me have.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he had thus spoken, he shewed them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hands and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " feet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And while they yet believed not for joy, and wondered, he said unto them, Have ye here any meat?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they gave him a piece of a broiled fish, and of an honeycomb.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he took ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and did eat before them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, These ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the words which I spake unto you, while I was yet with you, that all things must be fulfilled, which were written in the law of Moses, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the prophets, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the psalms, concerning me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then opened he their understanding, that they might understand the scriptures,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said unto them, Thus it is written, and thus it behoved Christ to suffer, and to rise from the dead the third day:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And that repentance and remission of sins should be preached in his name among all nations, beginning at Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ye are witnesses of these things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "¶ And, behold, I send the promise of my Father upon you: but tarry ye in the city of Jerusalem, until ye be endued with power from on high.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "¶ And he led them out as far as to Bethany, and he lifted up his hands, and blessed them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.51",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.51",
      "verse": 51,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, while he blessed them, he was parted from them, and carried up into heaven.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.52",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.52",
      "verse": 52,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they worshipped him, and returned to Jerusalem with great joy:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.24.53",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:LUK.24.53",
      "verse": 53,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And were continually in the temple, praising and blessing God. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
